# Example (ontology v1.3): a pk:Concept standing for a governing mathematical law, carried three
# ways — human formula (skos:notation), Lean 4 source (skos:definition ^^pk:lean4), and the
# kernel-checked identifiers (pk:leanDeclaration / pk:leanTheorem / pk:leanVerified).
#
# Taken from MorphoEval's math-of-biology graph (morpholib/morphoeval/kg/math_of_biology.ttl,
# built by morphoeval/math_kg.py at commit fb234bc; the Lean module is
# morphoeval/lean/MathOfBiology.lean and checks with `lean MathOfBiology.lean`, 0 sorry).
# The claim that *uses* the law is a separate pk:Claim (<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/claim/morphoeval-wolfram-conus-textile-rule30>)
# linked here with dct:conformsTo; its credibility is carried by pk:Assessment instances, not by
# pk:leanVerified — the kernel check only establishes the Lean theorem as stated.

@prefix pk:     <https://w3id.org/probknow/ontology/> .
# (individuals below are written as full IRIs: Turtle prefixed names cannot contain the "/" of pkr:<kind>/<id>)
@prefix rdfs:   <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix xsd:    <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix skos:   <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#> .
@prefix dct:    <http://purl.org/dc/terms/> .
@prefix prov:   <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#> .
@prefix schema: <https://schema.org/> .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/math-of-biology> a pk:Concept, skos:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Validated Mathematics of Biological Form"@en ;
    skos:narrower <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/wolfram-conus-textile-rule30-1> .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/wolfram-conus-textile-rule30-1> a pk:Concept, skos:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Wolfram (1983, 1984) Rule 30 Boolean & GF(2) Algebraic Normal Form"@en ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    dct:description "Discrete chaotic generator of self-similar white triangular tents on Conus textile shells and OEIS A051023 center column | Variables: a_{t,i} ∈ {0, 1}: pigment state at mantle cell i and step t; ⊕: XOR; ∨: OR"@en ;
    dct:source "Wolfram (1983) Rev. Mod. Phys. 55:601; (1984) Nature 311:419" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1103/RevModPhys.55.601>, <https://doi.org/10.1038/311419a0> ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Elementary Cellular Automata (GF(2))" ;

    # 1. the law as humans write it
    skos:notation "a_{t+1, i} = a_{t, i-1} ⊕ (a_{t, i} ∨ a_{t, i+1}) ≡ a_{t, i-1} + a_{t, i} + a_{t, i+1} + a_{t, i} a_{t, i+1} (mod 2)" ;

    # 2. the law as the proof assistant read it
    skos:definition """def rule30 (p q r : Bool) : Bool := bne p (q || r)
def rule30_anf (p q r : Bool) : Bool := bne (bne p q) (bne r (q && r))
theorem rule30_anf_equiv (p q r : Bool) : rule30 p q r = rule30_anf p q r := by
  cases p <;> cases q <;> cases r <;> rfl"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;

    # 3. what the kernel checked, and whether it accepted it
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.rule30" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.rule30_anf_equiv" ;
    pk:leanVerified "true"^^xsd:boolean ;

    # commit-pinned loci: the Lean module and the Python that implements the same law
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/fb234bc/morphoeval/lean/MathOfBiology.lean#L21-L37>,
                 <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/fb234bc/1984-wolfram-conus-textile-rule30.py#L96-L152> .

# The reproduction claim that rests on this law (abbreviated; see the MorphoEval graph for the full node).
<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/claim/morphoeval-wolfram-conus-textile-rule30> a pk:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Wolfram (1984) Rule 30 & Meinhardt–Klingler (1987) Conus textile pigmentation (Conus textile)"@en ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/wolfram-conus-textile-rule30-1> ;
    pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1038/311419a0> ;
    pk:weightOfEvidence "0.873"^^xsd:double .
